  "content": {
    "component": "news_article",
    "_uid": "2448-root",
    "title": "AKU's First Triage Simulation Course",
    "subtitle": null,
    "summary": "AKU's first-ever simulation-based Triage Management course was organised for nurses and technicians working in the hospital triage area.",
    "media": [
      {
        "_uid": "af9c674cd9295c3b",
        "component": "news_media",
        "role": "banner",
        "filename": "2448-BannerImage.jpg",
        "src": "/news-media/2448-BannerImage.jpg",
        "media_type": "image",
        "caption": null,
        "alt": "AKU's First Triage Simulation Course"
      }
    ],
    "body": {
      "type": "doc",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The Department of Emergency Medicine in collaboration with CIME conducted AKU's first-ever simulation-based Triage Management course for nurses and technicians working in the hospital triage area."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Triage is the processes of sorting and prioritizing patients for admission and treatment in the emergency department according to the severity of patients injury or illness. It ensures that the most critically ill patients get medical attention on priority, without delay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "A total of 20 participated in this course. It improved learners' clinical decision-making and equipped them with the knowledge and skills to deal with critical situations. It also enabled participants to experience the stress that occurs in a real-life situation and helped develop their resilience."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
